{
  "status": "applied",
  "key": "archive_format",
  "value": "zstd",
  "rationale": "zstd is the smallest of the three supported formats at 6 MB, beating gzip (9 MB) and zip (12 MB). A prior rejection of zstd existed because the downstream importer couldn't decode it, but that constraint has been lifted: the importer was upgraded today and its zstd compatibility tests now pass. With the blocking constraint gone, zstd is the clear choice for minimising nightly export size."
}
